  "notes": "Frozen S0 acceptance for the M5a-1 no-packet scenarios, transcribed from docs/mujoco-m5a-plan.md sections 5.3-5.4 before the first S0 run. Body/chassis attached-local relative translation 0.20 mm and rotation 0.20 deg are 50% of the 0.40 mm gap and the predicted 0.4 deg arrest. The signed world-z drop bound is 25% of the 0.40 mm gap and fails downward and upward; the positive downward drop max(0,-dz) is reported separately. 0.0715 N is 5% of the 145.89 g hanging group and 0.20 s is the longest allowed sustained load. chassis/floor 1 mm and 0.20 deg bound the analytic floor contact. Body and lip speeds are <=1 mm/s at the worst hold sample. 0.2 mm peak penetration is the numerical validity bound, not a product tolerance: a breach makes the dynamics INCONCLUSIVE, never a physical FAIL. The 20% near-threshold band is enabled, so a passing value within 20% of a bound is INCONCLUSIVE. contact_duration is the accepted generic whole-run summed-normal-force metric at integration-step resolution; it takes window=end and has no phase fields, so its window is the whole run and not the hold phase.",
